From 49b9d32478b827aa62f173af7a54be8ff50d8582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:06:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(documenteditor): Word font and paragraph controls

- Font name list with Word's sections: Theme Fonts (heading and body
  fonts, applied as theme references, shown in their own face when
  installed), Recently Used Fonts, All Fonts.
- Font size list of Word (8 ... 10.5, 11, 12 ... 72).
- Highlight colours: Word's 15 colours in Word order, 5 x 3, and
  "No Color" (white removed).
- Line spacing: "Line Spacing Options..." opens the Paragraph dialog
  instead of the right panel; icons on Add/Remove Space Before/After.
- Borders: "Borders and Shading..." at the end of the menu (paragraph
  borders and fill).
- Paragraph dialog: Alignment, Outline level and Direction on their own
  rows, as in Word.
Change Case (5 options), font colour (theme and standard colours, More
colors) and the bullet and numbering libraries with previews already
matched Word and are unchanged. Toolbar view: only the highlight
palette (colours, width). Strings in en, fr, de, es, it, pt, pt-pt, nl,
ru, pl, ja, zh.

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
